name Gravity well
recipe tier=1 X2p0 Y1p1
bench 1
root 65.4064
layer bed gravitic/gravitic_synth_00004 7 0.0000 3001 level=0.18000 attack=0.60000 release=1.00000 pitch=0.15000 cutoff=0.60000 echo=0.00000 reverb=0.25000 drive=0.00000 loop=1.00000 sines=1.00000 residual=1.00000 lfo_rate=0.35000 lfo>cut=0.00000 keyed=1 file=gravitic/gravitic_synth_00004.ogg
layer sub gravitic/gravitic_synth_00006 7 0.0000 3002 level=0.25000 attack=1.20000 release=1.50000 pitch=-4.85000 cutoff=0.60000 reverb=0.00000 loop=1.00000 sines=1.00000 residual=0.60000 keyed=1 file=gravitic/gravitic_synth_00006.ogg
layer cloud cloud 0 0.0000 3007 level=0.30000 attack=1.00000 release=1.50000 pitch=3.00000 cutoff=0.60000 reverb=0.80000 voices=6.00000 gather=1.00000 drift=0.20000 timbre=0.20000 chord=1.00000 sub=0.00000 keyed=1
layer tide gravitic/gravitic_slow_rising-falling_loop_00001 5 0.0000 3008 level=0.20000 attack=0.80000 release=1.20000 pitch=0.00000 cutoff=0.55000 loop=1.00000 keyed=2 file=gravitic/gravitic_slow_rising-falling_loop_00001.ogg
bind orb.radius tide cutoff 0.4 0.7
note Gravity well (tier I): X n2 p0 . Y n1 p1, a figure of eight. Root and root: the colour is the cloud's power chord at C3 and the
note sub coming up to full mass; the tide loop breathes with the orb. The voices are not listed: they keep following the chord tones.
